# SMF recipe: permission-normaliser exceptions (slice 6B flag 1).
# Read by the app container's init after its uniform pass; format:
#   <octal mode> <path relative to the app-data volume>
# Settings.php and its backup hold the database password. The
# uniform pass would leave them group-shared at 0664; the recipe
# keeps them at 0660 - still writable by the application (SMF's
# admin panel edits Settings.php) and manageable by the owner
# through the owner group, but never readable by other accounts
# on the host.
0660 www/Settings.php
0660 www/Settings_bak.php
